; exclude_integer_k2_model: EXCLUDE on an integer model with k = 2 raises
; NonBinaryModel.
;
; With k = 2 the integer domain is {0, 1}, so x^2 = x would hold, but
; spec/xqvm/SPEC.md makes the check follow the declared domain: only a model
; allocated by BQMX passes. This vector pins that rule; build such a model
; with BQMX instead.

PUSH 4
PUSH 2
XQMX r0          ; integer model, k = 2, 4 variables
PUSH 0           ; i
PUSH 1           ; j
PUSH 5           ; penalty
EXCLUDE r0
HALT
